[38;2;124;124;124m1. Moise's theorem (1952): Every topological 3-manifold can be triangulated, and[0m[38;2;124;124;124many two triangulations have a common refinement. This shows that every [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtopological 3-manifold has a PL structure, and the PL structure is unique.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m2. The relationship between PL structures and smooth structures in dimension 3: [0m[38;2;124;124;124mIn dimension 3, every PL manifold admits a unique smooth structure. This is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mbecause the obstruction groups vanish.[0m

